// This file never borrows anything, so `fmod` is an ordinary name here and it
// uses it for a variable - while calling a function from borrows.shl, which
// does borrow it.
//
// Resolve merges a pulled file's borrows into this program so that the pulled
// function's own calls resolve. If rule 3 were keyed on that merged list, this
// program would be refused for a clause it never wrote - and the app, which has
// one file and no merging, would disagree about which programs are legal. The
// `own` flag on Program::Borrowed is what keeps the two apart, and this is what
// says so.
fun <> = main() {
  real fmod : 99.5
  ? fmod
  ? wrapped(7.5, 2.0)
}
